This project continues two earlier projects by the same author, both
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  - doc-ollama-summarizer
    https://github.com/chemysterium/doc-ollama-summarizer

  - zotero-ollama-summarizer
    https://github.com/chemysterium/zotero-ollama-summarizer

Code carried over from them lives in extract.py (the .docx walker),
render.py (the LaTeX-to-Unicode conversion and Markdown list repair),
summarize.py (the prompts, language handling and map-reduce structure) and
zotero_source.py (item and collection resolution, note handling).

All three projects were written by the author together with Claude Code.

What changed here, relative to those two projects:

  - The two tools were merged into one CLI with selectable sources: a file,
    a folder, a Zotero item, a Zotero collection, or a whole Zotero library.
  - The model backend was changed from Ollama to LM Studio. Ollama's
    "think": false is replaced by LM Studio's reasoning_effort: "none", with
    a fallback for builds that reject the parameter.
  - Per-page OCR was added, using a vision model to read pages that have no
    text layer, and stitching them back together with the pages that do.
  - Markdown export was added as a first-class action that runs without any
    summarization.
  - Chunk sizes are now derived from the context length the model is actually
    loaded with, read from LM Studio's API, rather than being a constant.
  - Support was added for reading a Zotero library through Zotero's local,
    read-only API instead of the web API.
